# Module development (short rule)

**Full templates, examples, troubleshooting:** `docs/guides/MODULE_DEVELOPMENT_GUIDE.md`  
**Certification / lifecycle:** `memory-bank/moduleSpecs.md` + `.cursor/rules/module-interoperability.mdc`  
**AI system detail:** `memory-bank/aiContextSystem.md`  
**Notification metadata:** `docs/guides/NOTIFICATION_METADATA_GUIDE.md`

## Interoperability (non-negotiable)

- Same contract for built-in and marketplace modules: **`authorize → execute → emit normalized activity → notify/realtime`**; never emit on failed/unauthorized actions.
- Tenant scope on every persisted path; activity vs analytics separated; realtime membership proven before join/emit.
- Partner pipeline: `docs/guides/THIRD_PARTY_MODULE_DEVELOPER_GUIDE.md`, `docs/guides/THIRD_PARTY_MODULE_PIPELINE_SOURCE_OF_TRUTH.md`.

## Business workspace hub (prevent dashboard fallback)

Every business module needs:

1. **`[Module]WorkspaceLanding.tsx`** under `web/src/components/[module]/`.
2. **Switch** in `web/src/components/business/BusinessWorkspaceContent.tsx` for `case '[moduleId]':`.
3. **Icon + display name** in `web/src/components/BrandedWorkDashboard.tsx` (`getModuleIcon`, `getModuleName`).

Build the **hub first**, then deep pages. See long reference for templates.

## AI context

- Every module **must** ship a real **`ModuleAIContext`** (purpose, category, keywords, patterns, concepts, entities, actions, **`contextProviders`**).
- At least one **`/api/.../ai/context/...`** provider: auth’d, fast, bounded result sets — see `registerBuiltInModules.ts` patterns.

## AI action executors

If the module supports AI-driven writes, register an executor / supported operations per platform patterns (see long reference). Read-only modules may omit.

## Notifications

- Types: **`[module]_[event]`**; use **`NotificationService.createNotification`**; manifest **`notifications`** metadata required for discovery.
- Update **`web/src/app/notifications/page.tsx`** and **`web/src/api/notifications.ts`** when adding types (see `NOTIFICATION_METADATA_GUIDE.md`).

## Global trash

User-facing deletes: **`trashedAt` soft delete**, list queries exclude trashed, integrate **`trashController`** / **`useGlobalTrash`** — no hard delete for user data except documented exceptions. Details in long reference.

## Manifest

Ship complete manifest including **`aiContext`** and **`notifications`** when applicable; permissions and dependencies accurate for marketplace.

## Approval / review

- **A)** `moduleSpecs.md` certification (permissions, scoping, activity events, realtime, notifications, AI when exposed).  
- **B)** Product bar: hub works, providers fast, authZ, trash, tests, docs — long reference checklist.

